{
  "id": "DEU.20",
  "number": "20",
  "bookId": "DEU",
  "reference": "Deuteronomy 20",
  "verseCount": 20,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "20",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "DEU 20"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "20",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“When you go forth to war against your enemies, and see horses and chariots and an army larger than your own, you shall not be afraid of them; for the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God is with you, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when you draw near to the battle, the priest shall come forward and speak to the people, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and shall say to them, ‘Hear, O Israel, you draw near this day to battle against your enemies: let not your heart faint; do not fear, or tremble, or be in dread of them; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "for the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God is he that goes with you, to fight for you against your enemies, to give you the victory.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the officers shall speak to the people, saying, ‘What man is there that has built a new house and has not dedicated it? Let him go back to his house, lest he die in the battle and another man dedicate it. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And what man is there that has planted a vineyard and has not enjoyed its fruit? Let him go back to his house, lest he die in the battle and another man enjoy its fruit. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And what man is there that has betrothed a wife and has not taken her? Let him go back to his house, lest he die in the battle and another man take her.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the officers shall speak further to the people, and say, ‘What man is there that is fearful and fainthearted? Let him go back to his house, lest the heart of his fellows melt as his heart.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when the officers have make an end of speaking to the people, then commanders shall be appointed at the head of the people.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“When you draw near to a city to fight against it, offer terms of peace to it. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And if its answer to you is peace and it opens to you, then all the people who are found in it shall do forced labor for you and shall serve you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But if it makes no peace with you, but makes war against you, then you shall besiege it; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and when the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God gives it into your hand you shall put all its males to the sword, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but the women and the little ones, the cattle, and everything else in the city, all its spoil, you shall take as booty for yourselves; and you shall enjoy the spoil of your enemies, which the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God has given you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thus you shall do to all the cities which are very far from you, which are not cities of the nations here. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But in the cities of these peoples that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God gives you for an inheritance, you shall save alive nothing that breathes, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but you shall utterly destroy them, the Hittites and the Amorites, the Canaanites and the Perizzites, the Hivites and the Jebusites, as the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God has commanded; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "that they may not teach you to do according to all their abominable practices which they have done in the service of their gods, and so to sin against the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“When you besiege a city for a long time, making war against it in order to take it, you shall not destroy its trees by wielding an axe against them; for you may eat of them, but you shall not cut them down. Are the trees in the field men that they should be besieged by you? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 20:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Only the trees which you know are not trees for food you may destroy and cut down that you may build siegeworks against the city that makes war with you, until it falls.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.20.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.20.20"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "DEU.21",
    "number": "21",
    "bookId": "DEU"
  },
